e><div class="b-gray400 bb pen my16"></div></div><div class="fdc jcb"><article class="grid col1-min"><div class="f fdc col1 row1 sy8 mr8 jce"><div class="owa c-black tertiary fs16 sm:fs18"><a href="/news/article/new-haven-motorcycle-crash-pond-southern-ct-22395759.php" data-link="native" class="tdn hover:o70 td300">Motorcyclist critically injured after crashing into New Haven pond, police say</a></div></div><div class="grid row2 sy8 col1span2"><a href="/news/article/new-haven-motorcycle-crash-pond-southern-ct-22395759.php" data-link="native" class="c-gray700 m0 abstract fs16 lh13 none tdn hover:o70 td300"><div data-block-type="text" data-server-side-rendered="true" class="r12zgbl0 ruduv2y">Police said the motorcyclist was rescued from the water by first responders and bystanders. </div></a></div><div class="block col2 row1 x90px xs:x120px sm:x180px lg:x88px ml8"><a href="/news/article/new-haven-motorcycle-crash-pond-southern-ct-22395759.php" data-link="native" class=""><div class="rel x100 block"><picture><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 1048px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/54/31/02/28414141/3/ratio3x2_80.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(max-width: 1047px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/54/31/02/28414141/3/ratio3x2_160.webp"/><img alt="File photo of a New Haven police cruiser. Police said a motorcyclist was critically injured early Wednesday when they crashed into a pond near Southern Connecticut State University." loading="lazy" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/54/31/02/28414141/3/ratio3x2_80.jpg 80w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/54/31/02/28414141/3/ratio3x2_160.jpg 160w" sizes="160px" style="aspect-ratio:3 / 2" class="x100 y100 opc bgpc ofcv bgscv block bg-gray200 mnh0px fill"/></picture></div></a></div></article><div class="b-gray400 bb pen my16"></div></div><div class="fdc jcb"><article class="grid col1-min"><div class="f fdc col1 row1 sy8 mr8 jce"><div class="owa c-black tertiary fs16 sm:fs18"><a href="/news/article/ct-new-haven-amarante-sea-cliff-22395111.php" data-link="native" class="tdn hover:o70 td300">New Haven&#x27;s Amarante&#x27;s Sea Cliff is for sale, after 64 years in one family</a></div></div><div class="grid row2 sy8 col1span2"><a href="/news/article/ct-new-haven-amarante-sea-cliff-22395111.php" data-link="native" class="c-gray700 m0 abstract fs16 lh13 none tdn hover:o70 td300"><div data-block-type="text" data-server-side-rendered="true" class="r12zgbl0 ruduv2y">Opened as the Sea Cliff well "Sonny" Amarante took it over, Amarante's has long been a popular spot along Connecticut's shoreline.</div></a></div><div class="block col2 row1 x90px xs:x120px sm:x180px lg:x88px ml8"><a href="/news/article/ct-new-haven-amarante-sea-cliff-22395111.php" data-link="native" class=""><div class="rel x100 block"><picture><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 1048px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/67/07/56/31226778/5/ratio3x2_80.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(max-width: 1047px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/67/07/56/31226778/5/ratio3x2_160.webp"/><img alt="A bird&#x27;s eye view of Amarante&#x27;s Sea Cliff at 62 Cove St. in New Haven&#x27;s Morris Cove section, which is listed for sale 64 years after Andy &quot;Sonny&quot; Amarante bought it in 1962." loading="lazy" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/67/07/56/31226778/5/ratio3x2_80.jpg 80w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/67/07/56/31226778/5/ratio3x2_160.jpg 160w" sizes="160px" style="aspect-ratio:3 / 2" class="x100 y100 opc bgpc ofcv bgscv block bg-gray200 mnh0px fill"/></picture></div></a></div></article><div class="b-gray400 bb pen my16"></div></div><div class="fdc jcb"><article class="grid col1-min"><div class="f fdc col1 row1 sy8 mr8 jce"><div class="owa c-black tertiary fs16 sm:fs18"><a href="/news/article/new-haven-ct-election-complaint-dismissed-22394819.php" data-link="native" class="tdn hover:o70 td300">Election officials dismiss claim New Haven candidate traded meals for votes</a></div></div><div class="grid row2 sy8 col1span2"><a href="/news/article/new-haven-ct-election-complaint-dismissed-22394819.php" data-link="native" class="c-gray700 m0 abstract fs16 lh13 none tdn hover:o70 td300"><div data-block-type="text" data-server-side-rendered="true" class="r12zgbl0 ruduv2y">A state commission dismissed the complaint after an investigation did not establish any evidence for the allegations.</div></a></div><div class="block col2 row1 x90px xs:x120px sm:x180px lg:x88px ml8"><a href="/news/article/new-haven-ct-election-complaint-dismissed-22394819.php" data-link="native" class=""><div class="rel x100 block"><picture><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 1048px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/12/04/75/19418995/4/ratio3x2_80.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(max-width: 1047px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/12/04/75/19418995/4/ratio3x2_160.webp"/><img alt="Owners Sandra and Miguel Pittman outside their popular Sandra&#x27;s Next Generation restaurant in New Haven, Conn. on Sunday, May 10, 2020. " loading="lazy" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/12/04/75/19418995/4/ratio3x2_80.jpg 80w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/12/04/75/19418995/4/ratio3x2_160.jpg 160w" sizes="160px" style="aspect-ratio:3 / 2" class="x100 y100 opc bgpc ofcv bgscv block bg-gray200 mnh0px fill"/></picture></div></a></div></article><div class="b-gray400 bb pen my16"></div></div><div class="fdc jcb"><article class="grid col1-min"><div class="f fdc col1 row1 sy8 mr8 jce"><div class="owa c-black tertiary fs16 sm:fs18"><a href="/news/article/west-haven-structure-fire-canton-street-wednesday-22394927.php" data-link="native" class="tdn hover:o70 td300">Backyard fire spreads to West Haven home, displaces 3</a></div></div><div class="grid row2 sy8 col1span2"><a href="/news/article/west-haven-structure-fire-canton-street-wednesday-22394927.php" data-link="native" class="c-gray700 m0 abstract fs16 lh13 none tdn hover:o70 td300"><div data-block-type="text" data-server-side-rendered="true" class="r12zgbl0 ruduv2y"> The incident is being investigated by the Fire Marshal's Office.</div></a></div><div class="block col2 row1 x90px xs:x120px sm:x180px lg:x88px ml8"><a href="/news/article/west-haven-structure-fire-canton-street-wednesday-22394927.php" data-link="native" class=""><div class="rel x100 block"><picture><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 1048px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/41/03/31068369/5/ratio3x2_80.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(max-width: 1047px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/41/03/31068369/5/ratio3x2_160.webp"/><img alt="A file photo of a West Haven firetruck. West Haven fire officials say crews from all three city fire districts responded to a blaze on Canton Street Wednesday." loading="lazy" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/41/03/31068369/5/ratio3x2_80.jpg 80w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/41/03/31068369/5/ratio3x2_160.jpg 160w" sizes="160px" style="aspect-ratio:3 / 2" class="x100 y100 opc bgpc ofcv bgscv block bg-gray200 mnh0px fill"/></picture></div></a></div></article></div></div></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>“It’s a really fun, exciting time within the party, within Hamden politics as a whole,” said Osmanu, who also serves as corresponding secretary for the DTC. “You have really young candidates, energized candidates … (that’s) going to change how we think about municipal politics.”</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>When DTC member Megan Goslin nominated Khan for the party endorsement last week, she called the young candidate the “future of our party,” someone who “has the experience and skills needed to make our school district a more equitable one.” (Goslin shared a written copy of her comments with the New Haven Register.)</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>“I think there’s so much opportunity here to be a force that is hopeful,” Khan said of her decision to run. “This is a community that has quite literally raised me.”</p></div><div class="pt16 sy16 bb bt b-gray300 mb32"><div class=""><p class="uiHeader11 f aic jcc ttu">Advertisement</p><p class="uiTextSmall f aic jcc">Article continues below this ad</p></div><div data-block-type="ad" data-small-id="Inline-1" data-large-id="Inline-3" data-unit="hnp-nhregister.com/article_dtc" class="f jcc mnh250px pb16 aic lg:f lg:jcc lg:mnh250px lg:pb16 lg:aic"></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>It would be an “honor” to represent that community, she said.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>As a student representative, Khan campaigned to make Eid al-Fitr a holiday on which  students would get the day off, she said, adding that about 50 or 60 Muslim students voiced support of the idea.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>It hasn’t happened yet. Khan thinks the district missed an opportunity.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>“We could have really uplifted and empowered the students doing that work,” she said. “That’s one change that makes our school more inviting.”</p></div><div class="pt16 sy16 bb bt b-gray300 mb32"><div class=""><p class="uiHeader11 f aic jcc ttu">Advertisement</p><p class="uiTextSmall f aic jcc">Article continues below this ad</p></div><div data-block-type="ad" data-small-id="Inline-2" data-large-id="Inline-4" data-unit="hnp-nhregister.com/article_dtc" class="f jcc mnh250px pb16 aic lg:f lg:jcc lg:mnh250px lg:pb16 lg:aic"></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>As a board member, Khan would revisit the district calendar, she said. She also would seek to increase student and family engagement with board matters, prioritize issues related to racism and hold “office hours” where constituents could speak with her, she said.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>For Khan, family and faith are two important forces in her life.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Her parents are Pakistani immigrants who “taught me to work hard, to put people that you love first and to never give up,” she said, calling those lessons her “guiding principles.”</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>A practicing Muslim, she also said that “a lot of what compels me to do this work is my faith, and the importance of justice, and of kindness.”</p></div><div class="pt16 sy16 bb bt b-gray300 mb32"><div class=""><p class="uiHeader11 f aic jcc ttu">Advertisement</p><p class="uiTextSmall f aic jcc">Article continues below this ad</p></div><div data-block-type="ad" data-small-id="Inline-3" data-large-id="Inline-5" data-unit="hnp-nhregister.com/article_dtc" class="f jcc mnh250px pb16 aic lg:f lg:jcc lg:mnh250px lg:pb16 lg:aic"></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Khan mentioned her teachers, too — though they may not all live in town, she hopes to represent their interests as a board member.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>“I’ve had so many loving teachers throughout my 13 years at Hamden Public Schools,” she said. “So many of them go all the way for their students.”</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Osmanu also found inspiration at Hamden High School.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Though he always had some interest in politics, it was an AP Goverment class that sparked his involvement, he said. Legislative Councilman Brad Macdowall was a guest speaker at the class, according to Osmanu, who said he volunteered on Macdowall’s campaign the  following summer.</p></div><div class="pt16 sy16 bb bt b-gray300 mb32"><div class=""><p class="uiHeader11 f aic jcc ttu">Advertisement</p><p class="uiTextSmall f aic jcc">Article continues below this ad</p></div><div data-block-type="ad" data-small-id="Inline-4" data-large-id="Inline-6" data-unit="hnp-nhregister.com/article_dtc" class="f jcc mnh250px pb16 aic lg:f lg:jcc lg:mnh250px lg:pb16 lg:aic"></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Then, during his senior year, Osmanu served as president of the Black and Hispanic Student Union, he said. He credited the group’s adviser, Lamond Battle, with mentoring him.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>“I think that’s kind of where I started to find my own way, you know, as a leader,” Osmanu said.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Incumbent Councilwoman Athena Gary, D-3, who will not seek reelection, nominated Osmanu to take her place.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>So far, unlike <a href="https://www.nhregister.com/metro/article/Hamden-mayor-introduces-slate-after-failing-to-16353478.php" data-link="native" class="">many other endorsed candidates</a>, no one has indicated they will challenge Osmanu to a Democratic primary, nor did the GOP nominate anyone to run in the 3rd District.</p></div><div class="pt16 sy16 bb bt b-gray300 mb32"><div class=""><p class="uiHeader11 f aic jcc ttu">Advertisement</p><p class="uiTextSmall f aic jcc">Article continues below this ad</p></div><div data-block-type="ad" data-small-id="Inline-5" data-large-id="Inline-7" data-unit="hnp-nhregister.com/article_dtc" class="f jcc mnh250px pb16 aic lg:f lg:jcc lg:mnh250px lg:pb16 lg:aic"></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>But Osmanu is  campaigning nonetheless. He feels it’s important to make connections with community members, he said, because he will need their support to get things done as a councilman.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>“I don’t think it’s really possible without them,” he said.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><em>
                  <p>meghan.friedmann@hearstmediact.com</p>
                </em></div><div class="pt16 sy16 bb bt b-gray300 mb32"><div class=""><p class="uiHeader11 f aic jcc ttu">Advertisement</p><p class="uiTextSmall f aic jcc">Article continues below this ad</p></div><div data-block-type="ad" data-small-id="Inline-6" data-large-id="Inline-8" data-unit="hnp-nhregister.com/article_dtc" class="f jcc mnh250px pb16 aic lg:f lg:jcc lg:mnh250px lg:pb16 lg:aic"></div></div><div></div><div></div><div></div><div></div><div></div><div class="y1px x100 abs bgn top"></div><div style="top:25%" class="y1px x100 abs bgn"></div><div style="top:50%" class="y1px x100 abs bgn"></div><div style="top:75%" class="y1px x100 abs bgn"></div><div class="y1px x100 abs bgn bottom"></div></article></div><div class="package"><span class="mb16 block"><span class="smallTimestamp lg:largeTimestamp pb1 c-gray600"><time dateTime="2021-08-03 06:00:46">Aug 3, 2021</time></span></span><div><div class="py16"><div class="grid template-row2a temp-col-60px-1fr mnh100 g16 sm:g24"><div class="f fdc jcc xs:jcs xs:pt8 col1span3"><div class="primarySm mb2 xs:mb8"><a href="https://www.nhregister.com/author/meghan-friedmann/" data-link="native" class="tdu tuo2px">Meghan Friedmann</a></div><div class="cardByline ttu c-gray600">Reporter</div></div><div class="row3 col1Span xs:row2 xs:col1span4 sm:col1Span xs:mt8 sm:mt0"><div data-server-side-rendered="true" class="r12zgbl0 ruduv2y deckSm fs16 c-gray700 sy16"><p>Meghan Friedmann is a former reporter with the New Haven Register.</p></div></div><span class="col1Span xs:col4 xs:jsfe"><div class="sx8 f"></div></span></div></div></div><div></div></div></div><div class="none lg:f mnw300px x300px fdc g40 jcb"><div class="package y100 none md:block"><div class="s top97"><div data-block-type="ad" data-large-id="A300" data-unit="hnp-nhregister.com/article_dtc" class="lg:f lg:jcc lg:mnh600px lg:ais"></div></div></div><div data-eid="collection-118387-mostPopular" class="package"><div class="f fdc sy24"><div class="f aic mb16"><div cla