house Point Park","excerpt":"Officials identified 96 trees throughout the park that were felled or badly damaged and 85 that are in need of \"significant pruning.\"","abstract":"\u003cp\u003eOfficials identified 96 trees throughout the park that were felled or badly damaged and 85 that are in need of \"significant pruning.\"\u003c/p\u003e","plainTextAbstract":"Officials identified 96 trees throughout the park that were felled or badly damaged and 85 that are in need of \"significant pruning.\"","displayedDate":"2026-08-19 10:03:30","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-19 10:03:30","elapsedTime":null,"authorName":null,"authorHref":null,"authors":[{"id":1511,"name":"Brian Zahn","title":"Reporter","url":"/author/brian-zahn/","credit":null,"image":{"id":null,"url":"https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/20/27/76/21069700/8/rawImage.jpg","base64":null,"width":1538,"height":2048,"guid":null,"dirPath":null,"alt":"photo Brian Zahn from article titled \"Lamont surveys damage at New Haven’s Lighthouse Point Park, rebuild to cost millions\"","title":"Brian Zahn"}}],"bylineObjects":[{"id":1511,"name":"Brian Zahn","title":"Reporter","url":"/author/brian-zahn/","credit":"Staff Writer","image":{"id":21069700,"url":null,"base64":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","width":1538,"height":2048,"guid":"photo_21069700","dirPath":"01/20/27/76/21069700/8","alt":"photo Brian Zahn from article titled \"Lamont surveys damage at New Haven’s Lighthouse Point Park, rebuild to cost millions\"","title":"Brian Zahn"}}],"eyebrow":{"isPublished":true,"linkText":"News","url":"/news/"},"badge":null,"image":{"url":"https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/67/07/11/31224431/5/rawImage.jpg","b64":null,"width":2048,"height":1365,"caption":{"plain":"Gov. Ned Lamont, left, and Mayor Justin Elicker, center, tour the damaged carousel with City Engineer Giovanni Zinn, right, at Lighthouse Point Park in New Haven, Conn., Tuesday, August 18, 2026. Lighthouse Point Park suffered severe damage in an overnight storm last week.","html1":null,"serializedReact":null},"loading":"lazy","external":null,"alt":"Gov. Ned Lamont, left, and Mayor Justin Elicker, center, tour the damaged carousel with City Engineer Giovanni Zinn, right, at Lighthouse Point Park in New Haven, Conn., Tuesday, August 18, 2026. Lighthouse Point Park suffered severe damage in an overnight storm last week.","title":"ne081726mulpplamont-200"},"collectionConfig":{"showLabels":false,"persistentTimestamp":false,"showEyebrows":true,"showPhoto":null,"showByline":false,"showTimestamp":false,"useImg":false,"blurb":null,"useBlurb":false,"hideBlurbOnMobile":false,"forceHideEyebrows":false,"noFollow":false},"displayedDateFormat":"LLL d","sponsored":null,"videoloop":null,"slideshowImages":null,"bizRelItem":null}]}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003e“It’s a really fun, exciting time within the party, within Hamden politics as a whole,” said Osmanu, who also serves as corresponding secretary for the DTC. “You have really young candidates, energized candidates … (that’s) going to change how we think about municipal politics.”\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"“It’s a really fun, exciting time within the party, within Hamden politics as a whole,” said Osmanu, who also serves as corresponding secretary for the DTC. “You have really young candidates, energized candidates … (that’s) going to change how we think about municipal politics.”"}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eWhen DTC member Megan Goslin nominated Khan for the party endorsement last week, she called the young candidate the “future of our party,” someone who “has the experience and skills needed to make our school district a more equitable one.” (Goslin shared a written copy of her comments with the New Haven Register.)\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"When DTC member Megan Goslin nominated Khan for the party endorsement last week, she called the young candidate the “future of our party,” someone who “has the experience and skills needed to make our school district a more equitable one.” (Goslin shared a written copy of her comments with the New Haven Register.)"}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003e“I think there’s so much opportunity here to be a force that is hopeful,” Khan said of her decision to run. “This is a community that has quite literally raised me.”\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"“I think there’s so much opportunity here to be a force that is hopeful,” Khan said of her decision to run. “This is a community that has quite literally raised me.”"}}}},{"__typename":"AdBlock","type":"ad","params":{"layout":null,"chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"code":null,"small":"Inline-1","large":"Inline-3","showInlineAdLabel":true,"adUnitPath":"hnp-nhregister.com/article_dtc"}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eIt would be an “honor” to represent that community, she said.\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"It would be an “honor” to represent that community, she said."}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eAs a student representative, Khan campaigned to make Eid al-Fitr a holiday on which  students would get the day off, she said, adding that about 50 or 60 Muslim students voiced support of the idea.\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"As a student representative, Khan campaigned to make Eid al-Fitr a holiday on which  students would get the day off, she said, adding that about 50 or 60 Muslim students voiced support of the idea."}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eIt hasn’t happened yet. Khan thinks the district missed an opportunity.\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"It hasn’t happened yet. Khan thinks the district missed an opportunity."}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003e“We could have really uplifted and empowered the students doing that work,” she said. “That’s one change that makes our school more inviting.”\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"“We could have really uplifted and empowered the students doing that work,” she said. “That’s one change that makes our school more inviting.”"}}}},{"__typename":"AdBlock","type":"ad","params":{"layout":null,"chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"code":null,"small":"Inline-2","large":"Inline-4","showInlineAdLabel":true,"adUnitPath":"hnp-nhregister.com/article_dtc"}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eAs a board member, Khan would revisit the district calendar, she said. She also would seek to increase student and family engagement with board matters, prioritize issues related to racism and hold “office hours” where constituents could speak with her, she said.\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"As a board member, Khan would revisit the district calendar, she said. She also would seek to increase student and family engagement with board matters, prioritize issues related to racism and hold “office hours” where constituents could speak with her, she said."}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eFor Khan, family and faith are two important forces in her life.\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"For Khan, family and faith are two important forces in her life."}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eHer parents are Pakistani immigrants who “taught me to work hard, to put people that you love first and to never give up,” she said, calling those lessons her “guiding principles.”\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"Her parents are Pakistani immigrants who “taught me to work hard, to put people that you love first and to never give up,” she said, calling those lessons her “guiding principles.”"}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eA practicing Muslim, she also said that “a lot of what compels me to do this work is my faith, and the importance of justice, and of kindness.”\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"A practicing Muslim, she also said that “a lot of what compels me to do this work is my faith, and the importance of justice, and of kindness.”"}}}},{"__typename":"AdBlock","type":"ad","params":{"layout":null,"chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"code":null,"small":"Inline-3","large":"Inline-5","showInlineAdLabel":true,"adUnitPath":"hnp-nhregister.com/article_dtc"}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eKhan mentioned her teachers, too — though they may not all live in town, she hopes to represent their interests as a board member.\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"Khan mentioned her teachers, too — though they may not all live in town, she hopes to represent their interests as a board member."}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003e“I’ve had so many loving teachers throughout my 13 years at Hamden Public Schools,” she said. “So many of them go all the way for their students.”\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"“I’ve had so many loving teachers throughout my 13 years at Hamden Public Schools,” she said. “So many of them go all the way for their students.”"}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eOsmanu also found inspiration at Hamden High School.\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"Osmanu also found inspiration at Hamden High School."}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eThough he always had some interest in politics, it was an AP Goverment class that sparked his involvement, he said. Legislative Councilman Brad Macdowall was a guest speaker at the class, according to Osmanu, who said he volunteered on Macdowall’s campaign the  following summer.\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"Though he always had some interest in politics, it was an AP Goverment class that sparked his involvement, he said. Legislative Councilman Brad Macdowall was a guest speaker at the class, according to Osmanu, who said he volunteered on Macdowall’s campaign the  following summer."}}}},{"__typename":"AdBlock","type":"ad","params":{"layout":null,"chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"code":null,"small":"Inline-4","large":"Inline-6","showInlineAdLabel":true,"adUnitPath":"hnp-nhregister.com/article_dtc"}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eThen, during his senior year, Osmanu served as president of the Black and Hispanic Student Union, he said. He credited the group’s adviser, Lamond Battle, with mentoring him.\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"Then, during his senior year, Osmanu served as president of the Black and Hispanic Student Union, he said. He credited the group’s adviser, Lamond Battle, with mentoring him."}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003e“I think that’s kind of where I started to find my own way, you know, as a leader,” Osmanu said.\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"“I think that’s kind of where I started to find my own way, you know, as a leader,” Osmanu said."}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eIncumbent Councilwoman Athena Gary, D-3, who will not seek reelection, nominated Osmanu to take her place.\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"serializedReact":{"type":"p","key":null,"ref":null,"props":{"children":"Incumbent Councilwoman Athena Gary, D-3, who will not seek reelection, nominated Osmanu to take her place."}}}},{"__typename":"TextBlock","type":"text","params":{"layout":"","chapter":null,"chapterHeader":null,"html1":"\u003cp\u003eSo far, unlike \u003ca href=\"https://www.nhregister.com/metro/article/Hamden-mayor-introduces-slate-after-failing-to-16353478.php\"\u003emany other endorsed candidates\u003c/a\u003e, no one has indicated they will challenge Osmanu to a Democratic primary, nor did the GOP nominate anyone to run in the 3rd District.\u003c/p\u003e","isDropcap":false,"se